 "provenance": {
  "attrs": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - style, sides, backbone and cover material, colour and the detachable cover are the specification table of the FS Horizontal Cable Managers with Finger Duct datasheet (steel, portal id 6867); RoHS and ISO 9001 its Standards Compliance list; the four screws and cage nuts are step 1 of the FS Horizontal Cable Managers quick start guide V1.0 for CMH-SFDS1U and CMH-DFDS2U."
  },
  "backbone": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the side view puts the backbone 117 from one cover (its dimension) and so 115 from the other; it is drawn centred, 115.4 + 1.2 + 115.4, 1.6 mm from the dimension, so that one finger part serves both channels."
  },
  "backbone-holes": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - whether the backbone of the dual duct is pierced: the drawing draws it edge-on only, and gallery image 3 shows it dark through the open channel but for one light patch near the left end. Drawn solid; see the gap."
  },
  "bottom": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the bottom row of fingers is the top row again."
  },
  "capacity": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - FS states no cable capacity for CMH-DFDS2U in any document held (the steel finger duct datasheet has no capacity table and the portfolio gives dimensions only), so the 270 is worked out, not read. METHOD: the inside cross-section of both channels, the `duct` guide height by the depth from the front face of the backbone to the rear face of the cover on the side view of the steel finger duct datasheet, divided by 47.7 mm2 a Cat6 cable. 47.7 is the median of the mm2 a cable that FS's own Cat6 counts imply for CMH-SFD1U, CMH-DFD1U, CMH-SFD2U, CMH-BS-SFDS1U, CMH-BS-DFDABS2U, CMH-HD-SFDABS3U and 4U and CMH-UHD-SFDABS1U, 2U and 3U (38.7 to 82.8), rounded up to 0.1; the count is rounded down. CROSS-SECTION: 2 x (56.7 x 113.6) = 12882.2 mm2, and 12882.2 / 47.7 = 270.0. The count is of Cat6 24AWG and is marked as an estimate (`cable-capacity-estimated`)."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - THE BODY BETWEEN THE EARS. 482.6 over the ears, 465 between the hole centres; the cover and the duct between the ears read 537 px, 440.0. The ears, 20.5 each with three holes, are not drawn. Height 84.1 is the cover and the spec table, 103 px on both the front and the side view; the ears are 88 (2U). Depth 232 is the side view over both covers and the spec table."
  },
  "color": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - Color: Black, drawn in the shades CMH-SFDS1U reads off its renders."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - `positions` states where the ears bolt, for the Rack Builder. The ears are on the backbone, which stands 116 mm from each cover (the side view, 232 over both covers, datasheet page 5; FS dimensions 117 from a cover edge to the backbone). `at` is 116, so the part spans the rail. This states a placement; no dimension changed."
  },
  "fingers": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - ten fingers a row, the plan dimensioning 44.5 between the windows of two fingers and drawing the stems 54.3 px apart, 44.5; ten at that pitch run past the 440 cover, so 44.0 is taken and the row fills the body, as on CMH-SFDS1U. The moulding is the one CMH-SFDS1U carries: a 10.2 stem forking into two legs over a moulded block, a T head 39.4 wide. The fork is drawn as the stem."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the cover, fitted, as the front view draws it: 440 x 84.1 with four hinge clips, two on the top edge at 75.4 and 342.5 from the left end and two on the bottom below them. The finger rows are 9.0 thick, 4.7 in from the top and bottom of the cover, read off the side view (rails 4.9 to 13.9 and 70.5 to 80.3 from the top) and made symmetric. The `duct` guide is the 56.7 between the rows."
  },
  "full-depth": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "`full-depth: false` - a dual-sided duct bolts to the front rails with its fingers facing both ways: it stands 116 mm to each side of its backbone (the side view, 232 over both covers), so it serves the face it is bolted to and the space just behind the rails, and at 232 mm it does not reach the rear rails of a rack. The rear face of its two rack units stays free for another part."
  },
  "guides": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - one duct on each of the front and rear views, the channel between the finger rows, run across the rack."
  },
  "left": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the side view: two finger rows each side of the backbone, the covers at both ends. Both channels are open at the ends."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "FIGURES FROM THE VENDOR DRAWING. The FS Horizontal Cable Managers with Finger Duct datasheet (steel, portal id 6867) carries a technical drawing of CMH-DFDS2U: a plan, an isometric, the front and a side view. The embedded image (1437 x 779) is 1.2205 px/mm across the 482.6, 1.216 down the 88, 1.224 along the 232 and 1.225 down the 84.1 of the cover: orthographic, to about a millimetre. The renders of #220087 are the second reading; their backgrounds are transparent and were laid on white before measuring."
  },
